course: dictionary
lesson: 1462
title: Reading clues about a giant bird
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A context clue is a hint in the words around an unknown word. «The cassowary is a big flightless bird with a crest.» You may not know flightless, but the words big bird tell you it is a bird, and the word flightless is a clue. A bird that cannot fly is flightless.
explain: Use your clues to test a meaning. «It has sharp dagger-like claws and can be dangerous if people get too close.» Dagger-like tells you the claws are sharp, and the warning tells you the bird is not safe to be near. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some clues come from the whole text. In the sentence «Cassowaries swallow fruit whole and spread the seeds of over 200 kinds of plants in their droppings», the word spread is not about butter or jam. The seeds are moved far away, so spread means scatter them.
fact: Flightless means unable to fly.
fact: A casque is a tall, hard crest on the head of a cassowary.
fact: A cassowary is a very large bird from the rainforests of north-eastern Australia and New Guinea.
fact: Cassowaries eat fallen fruit and spread seeds far away in their droppings, which helps rainforest trees grow.
fact: Fed cassowaries lose their fear of people, so they must never be fed.
exercise: «The cassowary is a big flightless bird with a crest.» What does flightless mean? | Has feathers that glow | Very fast in the air | Lives under the sea | *Cannot fly
exercise: «Cassowaries swallow fruit whole and spread the seeds of over 200 kinds of plants.» What does spread mean here? | Stop the seeds from growing | Plant the seeds in a neat row in a pot | Eat the seeds slowly | *Scatter the seeds far and wide
exercise: «It can be dangerous, so people should never go close.» Find and copy the one word that means not safe. | people | close | should | *dangerous
test: «It has sharp dagger-like claws.» What does dagger-like suggest? | Soft and fluffy | *Sharp, like the blade of a knife | Bright and shiny like glass | Long and bendy like a rope
test: Safety signs say «Cassowary Crossing» and «be cass-o-wary». What does the pun be cass-o-wary mean? | *Be careful of the cassowary | Be quiet and still in the rainforest | Be happy when you see a cassowary | Be a cassowary and learn to fly
exam: «Fed cassowaries lose their fear and can kick if fed or cornered.» Why must people never feed a cassowary? | Birds only kick when they are happy | *Fed birds lose their fear and can kick | Fed birds grow too fast to fly | Food makes their feathers fall out
